            <fr:title text="AllToAll is a quarter of an AllGather">AllToAll is a quarter of an AllGather</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="anki">1786546735861</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p><fr:link href="/T470/" title="AllToAll" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/T470/" display-uri="T470" type="local">AllToAll</fr:link>: signature, when it shows up, and why is it cheaper than an <fr:link href="/VSDZ/" title="AllGather" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/VSDZ/" display-uri="VSDZ" type="local">AllGather</fr:link>?</html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  <html:strong>Signature</html:strong> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[[A, B_X] \to  [A_X, B]]]></fr:tex> — a sharded transposition, which <html:em>moves</html:em> a subscript from one logical axis to another.

  <html:strong>When</html:strong>: never out of a sharded matmul. It is for resharding between regions of a computation with incompatible layouts — classically MoE routing.

  <html:strong>Cost</html:strong> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[V \cdot  \max (A, B, C, \ldots ) / (4 N W_{\mathrm {ici}})]]></fr:tex>; on a 1D mesh that is <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[V / (4 W_{\mathrm {ici}})]]></fr:tex>, a <html:strong>quarter</html:strong> of an AllGather, and it scales down further in 2D+ with the shortest axis.

  <html:strong>Why cheaper</html:strong>, as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[2 \times  2]]></fr:tex>: each device need not send its <html:em>whole</html:em> shard everywhere, so the sum becomes <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[D + (D-1) + \cdots  + 1]]></fr:tex> instead of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[D]]></fr:tex> repeated <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[D]]></fr:tex> times — a factor of 2. And bidirectionality buys <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[4\times ]]></fr:tex> here rather than the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[2\times ]]></fr:tex> it buys an AllGather, since blocks travel at most <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[D/2]]></fr:tex> hops in either direction. Equivalently: two random nodes on a <fr:link href="/UEA0/" title="Ring topology" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/UEA0/" display-uri="UEA0" type="local">ring</fr:link> are about <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[N/4]]></fr:tex> hops apart.
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors>
